        "timestamp": 1773582411,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump urges allies to send warships to Strait of Hormuz Middle East Issued on: 15/03/2026 - 14:46 President Donald Trump has threatened to get the Strait of Hormuz opened \"one way or another\" and has called on a number of countries including France, the United Kingdom and China to send ships to the area to overcome Iran's blockade on the vital trade artery. It comes as global oil supplies are skyrocketing and supply continues to be strangled with Iran blockading the strait and targeting the Gulf's energy infrastructure in retaliation to US strikes. Story by Shirli Sitbon and Eliza Herbert. Are Iran's retaliatory strikes across the Gulf region affecting the US' war strategy? 15/03/2026 Middle East Could Nigeria become an alternative oil supplier to the Middle East? 15/03/2026 Africa Who is running Iran? The regime's new strongmen 15/03/2026 Middle East What role is oil playing in the war in the Middle East and what's at stake? 15/03/2026 Analysis Middle East Gaza hit by strongest sandstorm in over five years 15/03/2026 Middle East Qatar, Kuwait, UAE... Iranian reprisals disrupt daily life across the Gulf 15/03/2026 Middle East Undercover in Iran: How French spies gather Intelligence in the Middle East 15/03/2026 Middle East Israel pounds Beirut, deepening the humanitarian crisis in Lebanon 15/03/2026 Middle East Donald Trump says will open Strait of Hormuz \"one way or another\" 15/03/2026 Middle East"
